1
00:00:01,905 --> 00:00:08,965
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا * أمَّا بَعْد

2
00:00:10,065 --> 00:00:15,455
This is our second session, on the life of Sayyedina(سيدنا) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

3
00:00:16,166 --> 00:00:25,920
We talked in our previous session on some background information and an introduction to this series.

4
00:00:26,556 --> 00:00:30,457
Now we'll talk about the family of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

5
00:00:32,034 --> 00:00:38,798
His first wife was Qateela Bint Abdul Uzzah(قتيله بنت عبد العزة), whom he divorced, in the time of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة).

6
00:00:40,056 --> 00:00:43,504
There's a difference of opinion on whether she later became a Muslim or not

7
00:00:44,665 --> 00:00:48,536
and she was the mother of Asmaa(اسماء) and Abdullah(عبدالله).

8
00:00:49,133 --> 00:00:53,534
So Qateela(قتيله) was the mother of Asmaa(اسماء) and Abdullah(عبدالله), that's his first wife.

9
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:57,345
He was also married to Umm Romaan Bint Aamir(ام رومان بنت عامر)

10
00:00:58,971 --> 00:01:01,006
she was one of the early Muslims.

11
00:01:01,689 --> 00:01:07,541
And she was the mother of Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) and Ayeshaرضي الله عنهم.

12
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:11,541
His third wife was Asmaa Bint Umais(اسماء بنت عميس),

13
00:01:11,581 --> 00:01:14,710
now Asmaa Bint Umais(اسماء بنت عميس) was the wife of Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر ابن ابي طالب)

14
00:01:14,909 --> 00:01:18,596
 the brother of Ali(علي), the cousin of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

15
00:01:19,418 --> 00:01:24,042
And Asmaa(اسماء) made Hijrah(هجرة) with her husband Jafar(جعفر) to Abyssinia

16
00:01:24,613 --> 00:01:30,052
and we know that Jafar(جعفر) is the Ameer(امير) of the Muslims, in Abyssinia

17
00:01:31,646 --> 00:01:33,622
and they stayed there for a very long time.

18
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:38,121
And they only came back during the time of Ghazwat Khaybar(غزوة خيبر),

19
00:01:39,348 --> 00:01:45,354
which was towards the latter part of the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ in Madina.

20
00:01:46,738 --> 00:01:50,576
And then Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر ابن ابي طالب) was second in command in the Battle of Mu'ta(مؤته),

21
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:54,095
Rasool Allah ﷺ later on sent him in the eighth year of Hijrah(هجرة),

22
00:01:55,699 --> 00:02:00,152
as second in command after Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) in the Battle of Mu'ta(مؤته).

23
00:02:00,176 --> 00:02:01,996
So, when Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) was killed.

24
00:02:02,465 --> 00:02:06,802
The one, who assumed leadership after him was Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفرابن ابي طالب).

25
00:02:07,895 --> 00:02:11,973
And he was carrying the flag or the banner of war.

26
00:02:12,273 --> 00:02:15,435
So his right hand was cut, he held it with the left hand

27
00:02:15,817 --> 00:02:20,215
the left hand was cut, so he held it with whatever was left from his arms

28
00:02:20,923 --> 00:02:22,542
that was also chopped.

29
00:02:22,979 --> 00:02:26,371
 So he hugged it, until he fell down dead in the end.

30
00:02:27,166 --> 00:02:35,428
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said, Allahسبحانه وتعالى has replaced his two arms with two wings for him to fly with them in paradise.

31
00:02:36,743 --> 00:02:39,880
So, his wife Asmaa Bint Umais(اسماء بنت عميس) was widowed.

32
00:02:40,415 --> 00:02:46,555
It was the tradition of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, not to leave any women single.

33
00:02:47,812 --> 00:02:54,573
If a woman is divorced, if a woman is widowed or if a woman didn't get married early

34
00:02:55,149 --> 00:02:59,144
the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would not leave such a sister alone.

35
00:02:59,657 --> 00:03:04,246
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه married Asmaa Bint Umais(اسماء بنت عميس)

36
00:03:05,723 --> 00:03:11,229
and she was the mother of Muhammad Ibn Abi Bakr(محمد ابن ابي بكر).

37
00:03:13,616 --> 00:03:20,366
The fourth wife of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was Habiba Bint Kharijah(حبيبه بنت خارجه).

38
00:03:21,092 --> 00:03:27,028
And she is from among Al-Ansaar(الانصار), specifically from the tribe of Al-Khazraj رضي الله عنهم.

39
00:03:27,965 --> 00:03:35,685
And she used to live in a place called As-Sanhe(السنح), which is, if we would say the suburbs of Madina.

40
00:03:36,391 --> 00:03:39,587
 So, it was a little far away from the center of town.

41
00:03:40,112 --> 00:03:43,395
And that's where Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) was, when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

42
00:03:43,436 --> 00:03:47,777
So, that's why he came on late, after the news has already spread.

43
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:52,771
We'll talk about that, because he has spent that night with his wife in As-Sanhe(السنح),

44
00:03:53,348 --> 00:03:56,335
she was the mother of Umm Kalsoom Bint Abi Bakr(ام كلثوم بنت ابي بكر).

45
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:59,127
So these are the wives of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق).

46
00:03:59,217 --> 00:04:02,852
Again Qateela Bint Abd Ul Uzzah(قتيله بنت عبد العزة), Umm Romaan Bint Aamir(ام رومان بنت عامر)

47
00:04:03,130 --> 00:04:07,068
 Asmaa Bint Umais(اسماء بنت عميس) and Habiba Bint Kharijah(حبيبه بنت خارجه).

48
00:04:07,375 --> 00:04:11,750
His children, the eldest was Abdur Rahman Bin Abi Bakr(عبد الرحمن بن ابي بكر).

49
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:17,133
He became Muslim quite late compared to the rest of the family

50
00:04:17,767 --> 00:04:20,229
he was the last person among the family to become Muslim.

51
00:04:20,868 --> 00:04:23,571
In fact he fought against the Muslims in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

52
00:04:23,906 --> 00:04:32,510
Abdur Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr(عبد الرحمن بن ابي بكر) was known as one of the courageous and strong fighters of Quraish(قریش), that was his reputation.

53
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:36,379
He only became Muslim after Sulh Al-Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه).

54
00:04:37,473 --> 00:04:40,251
Then he had Abdullah Bin Abi Bakr رضي الله عنه

55
00:04:40,754 --> 00:04:46,840
and Abdullah(عبدالله), played a critical role in Al-Hijrah(الهجرة) and we'll talk about that.

56
00:04:47,456 --> 00:04:53,633
Now Abdullah Bin Abi Bakr(عبد الله بن ابي بكر) was injured by an arrow during the siege of At-Taef(الطائف).

57
00:04:54,407 --> 00:05:00,870
However, it didn't kill him immediately, he only died during the Khilafah(خلافة) of his father, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

58
00:05:00,959 --> 00:05:09,619
So, the injury was critical but he lived in that injured states for some time and then eventually he died.

59
00:05:10,093 --> 00:05:15,878
 So his death is considered Shahadah(شهادة) because it was due to the injury caused by that arrow.

60
00:05:17,193 --> 00:05:24,140
Later on, the story goes that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), he retained that arrow with him, he kept the arrow

61
00:05:25,157 --> 00:05:30,628
and when he was Khalifah(خليفه) and he met with the delegation from At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف).

62
00:05:31,265 --> 00:05:35,436
He brought out that arrow and he asked them, who does this arrow belong to?

63
00:05:36,625 --> 00:05:40,918
So one of them not knowing what was the reason of this question?

64
00:05:41,383 --> 00:05:46,356
He said, after he took a close look at the arrow, he said:

65
00:05:46,810 --> 00:05:49,861
This arrow is mine؛ I'm the one who sharpened it

66
00:05:50,201 --> 00:05:54,437
I'm the one who prepared it, I'm the one who stuck the feathers to it

67
00:05:54,676 --> 00:05:55,937
and I am the one who shot with it.

68
00:05:56,520 --> 00:06:00,850
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: And that's the arrow that killed my son, Abdullah(عبدالله).

69
00:06:02,575 --> 00:06:05,188
So the man said: Well, Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله),

70
00:06:05,309 --> 00:06:09,095
who has honored your son by me, killing him and making him a Shaheed(شَهِيد)

71
00:06:09,862 --> 00:06:13,084
and Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله) who has then guided me and made me a Muslim.

72
00:06:14,634 --> 00:06:19,761
Muhammad Ibn Abu Bakr(محمد إبن ابوبكر), and his mother was Asma Bint Umais(أسماءبنت عميس).

73
00:06:20,673 --> 00:06:24,316
Muhammad Ibn Abu Bakr(محمد إبن ابوبكر) was brought up by Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

74
00:06:25,079 --> 00:06:26,785
 because of the relationships.

75
00:06:26,809 --> 00:06:30,198
See Asma bint Umais(أسماءبنت عميس) was the ex-wife of his brother.

76
00:06:31,292 --> 00:06:35,535
So when she had her son from Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, Muhammad(محمد).

77
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:38,840
Ali ibn Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) is the one who raised him up

78
00:06:39,623 --> 00:06:41,500
and they had a very close relationship.

79
00:06:42,571 --> 00:06:48,500
Infact in the time of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), he appointed Muhammad(محمد) as his governor over Egypt.

80
00:06:49,791 --> 00:06:57,481
Asma bint Abi Bakr رضی اللہ عنھا the older daughter of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), she was older than Ayesha رضي الله عنها.

81
00:06:57,620 --> 00:07:01,407
Asma Bint Abi Bakr(أسماء بنت أبي بكر) also played a very important role in Al-Hijrah(ألهجرى).

82
00:07:01,825 --> 00:07:03,938
She was called Zaat An-Nataqain(ذات النطاقين),

83
00:07:04,653 --> 00:07:10,477
the woman of the two belts, and Nataq(نطاق) is a belt that woman used to use, on their waist.

84
00:07:11,028 --> 00:07:16,887
It's a belt made out of cloth, it was a piece of cloth that they would wrap on their waists.

85
00:07:17,410 --> 00:07:23,949
Now, when she was delivering food to Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in the cave,

86
00:07:24,726 --> 00:07:27,638
she didn't have anything to put the food in.

87
00:07:27,956 --> 00:07:32,337
So what she did is, she tied that belt into two pieces,

88
00:07:32,878 --> 00:07:37,823
and she put the food into those two pieces and delivered it to Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

89
00:07:38,221 --> 00:07:42,403
So it was Rasool Allah ﷺ, who called her, gave her the name of Zaat An-Nataqain(ذات النطاقين).

90
00:07:42,791 --> 00:07:47,288
This name was given to her by Rasool Allah ﷺ, Zaat An-Nataqain(ذات النطاقين).

91
00:07:47,328 --> 00:07:53,258
 Now Asma Bint Abi Bakr(أسماء بنت أبي بكر) got married to a Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام)

92
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:56,413
one of the 10 who were given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

93
00:07:57,127 --> 00:08:01,884
Az-Zubair Bin Awwam رضي الله عنه was a warrior.

94
00:08:02,677 --> 00:08:07,426
So he was a bit harsh with Asma Bint Abi Bakr رضي الله عنها

95
00:08:08,790 --> 00:08:14,496
and he would have her do a lot of laborious work at home.

96
00:08:16,155 --> 00:08:18,122
So she went and complained to her father.

97
00:08:19,495 --> 00:08:20,868
She said: My husband,

98
00:08:20,908 --> 00:08:22,741
and that was the nature of Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام),

99
00:08:22,781 --> 00:08:25,381
I mean Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام) was a tough man.

100
00:08:25,457 --> 00:08:33,770
One of his stories, he once hit, one of the enemy soldiers and he split him into two pieces.

101
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:41,451
And the sword went down after cutting the men into two pieces, and it cut the saddle of the horse.

102
00:08:41,603 --> 00:08:43,413
So the saddle fell from both sides.

103
00:08:43,873 --> 00:08:46,881
The Sahabah(صحابه), who saw that they said;

104
00:08:47,493 --> 00:08:50,082
You have a powerful sword, O Zubair(زبير).

105
00:08:50,594 --> 00:08:54,844
So Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام) responded by saying it is the arm that is powerful, not the sword.

106
00:08:56,348 --> 00:09:00,582
There was a well known Faris(فارس), warrior from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

107
00:09:01,113 --> 00:09:02,641
they used to call him, Al-Kabsh(ألكبش).

108
00:09:03,324 --> 00:09:05,363
He was big, well built fighter.

109
00:09:05,823 --> 00:09:11,613
He got into a duel with Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام) in one of the battles,

110
00:09:12,599 --> 00:09:17,243
and this man was covered in Iron, covered in armory from head to toe.

111
00:09:17,896 --> 00:09:24,221
So Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام) with his spear hit him in the opening for the eye.

112
00:09:24,245 --> 00:09:27,631
See that's the only place that is open, in this armory.

113
00:09:27,711 --> 00:09:32,407
He is covered in steel from head to toe with only small holes for him to see through.

114
00:09:33,669 --> 00:09:39,548
So Az-Zubair(ألزبير) hit him with the spear in that opening but the blade of the spear was big, so it couldn't go through.

115
00:09:40,612 --> 00:09:42,614
 So Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام) pushed it so hard.

116
00:09:42,997 --> 00:09:47,939
And then he stepped on it with his foot, until he got it through and it killed the man.

117
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:52,190
But when they pulled out the Spear, the blade which was a thick blade was bent.

118
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:57,323
Now when the Sahabah(صحابه) saw that, it was amazing, I mean you have this thick blade of steel bent.

119
00:09:58,083 --> 00:10:03,373
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه wanted to keep it as a souvenir and he gave it to him

120
00:10:03,959 --> 00:10:08,340
and when he died, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to keep it, so he kept it as a souvenir.

121
00:10:09,029 --> 00:10:12,144
And then it moved from Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان)

122
00:10:12,552 --> 00:10:17,179
and then later on, it was inherited by the son of Zubair(ألزبير), Abdullah(عبدلله), and he kept it with him, until he died.

123
00:10:17,514 --> 00:10:21,807
I mean as a memory from his father.

124
00:10:22,272 --> 00:10:26,276
So Asma Bint Abi Bakr(أسماء بنت أبي بكر) went to her father complaining about her husband.

125
00:10:27,421 --> 00:10:30,027
She said: He's having me to do all of this Labouress work,

126
00:10:30,898 --> 00:10:37,011
cleaning his house, taking care of his kids, grinding the flour

127
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:44,539
and then he has me feed his horse, take care of his horse, and all of that and it's too much for me,

128
00:10:45,108 --> 00:10:47,746
 she was asking for a servant and some help.

129
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:54,628
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه could have told her take him to court and ask for a divorce.

130
00:10:56,020 --> 00:10:57,043
But what he said.?

131
00:10:57,948 --> 00:11:06,345
He said: If a woman has a righteous husband, she will be his wife in Jannah(جنة).

132
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:11,242
So my daughter, be patient! My daughter be patient.

133
00:11:12,098 --> 00:11:18,795
Because Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, knew that Az-Zubair Bin Awwam is one of the 10 who are given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

134
00:11:19,981 --> 00:11:22,714
So it's an honor for his daughter to be with such a man.

135
00:11:23,194 --> 00:11:29,025
So he told her: Be patient! Be patient! And she was.

136
00:11:31,694 --> 00:11:40,629
Asma Bint Abi Bakr رضي الله عنها reached, actually she passed the age of 100 years

137
00:11:41,082 --> 00:11:46,161
without losing any of her mental abilities and without losing even one tooth,

138
00:11:46,543 --> 00:11:50,842
and she died in Makkah in year 73 of Al-Hijrah(هجرى).

139
00:11:51,776 --> 00:11:56,552
And she narrated 56 Ahadith(احاديث) of the Ahadith(احاديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

140
00:11:57,737 --> 00:12:03,897
Next, Ayesha(عائشه), the most beloved person, to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

141
00:12:05,212 --> 00:12:09,327
Ayesha رضي الله عنها, when Ash-Sha'abi(ألشعبي) would narrate her Hadith(حديث).

142
00:12:09,595 --> 00:12:15,043
He would say, this Hadith(حديث) is narrated by Al-Habiba Bint Al-Habib(ألحبيبة بنت ألحبيب),

143
00:12:15,603 --> 00:12:18,069
the beloved, the daughter of the Beloved.

144
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:22,988
She was beloved to Rasool Allah ﷺ and her father was beloved to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

145
00:12:23,359 --> 00:12:31,636
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he would be in a gathering, he would look the Sahabah(صحابه) in the eye and give them attention.

146
00:12:33,173 --> 00:12:35,672
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was a new Muslim

147
00:12:36,682 --> 00:12:42,870
and Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he would speak in a gathering he would look at Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and speak to him directly.

148
00:12:43,999 --> 00:12:47,518
So Amr Bin Al-Aas رضي الله عنه felt that Rasool Allah ﷺ loves me so much.

149
00:12:47,630 --> 00:12:52,368
I mean, he's looking at me out of all these people, it means, that he likes me.

150
00:12:53,269 --> 00:12:57,803
So Amr Bin Al-Aas رضي الله عنه later on, went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

151
00:12:58,284 --> 00:13:00,663
Who is the most beloved person to you?

152
00:13:01,245 --> 00:13:04,849
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Ayesha رضي الله عنها

153
00:13:05,753 --> 00:13:11,526
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: What about from among the men who is the most beloved from the men to you?

154
00:13:11,956 --> 00:13:13,527
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

155
00:13:13,656 --> 00:13:14,970
ومن الرجال أبوها

156
00:13:15,305 --> 00:13:17,248
And from among the men, her father.

157
00:13:18,125 --> 00:13:27,678
So Ayesha رضي الله عنها was the most beloved of the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ to him, after Khadeejah رضي الله عنها.

158
00:13:30,223 --> 00:13:34,477
Ayesha رضي الله عنها, she married Rasool Allah ﷺ at the age of six.

159
00:13:35,989 --> 00:13:46,074
It was the destiny of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ that He marries Ayesha رضي الله عنها to Rasool Allah ﷺ

160
00:13:46,845 --> 00:13:53,356
in order that she become the greatest woman's scholar of this Ummah(امة).

161
00:13:54,157 --> 00:14:00,338
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has destined that Ayesha رضي الله عنها will be the one,

162
00:14:00,735 --> 00:14:05,214
who will convey the Ahadith(احاديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ to Ummah(امة).

163
00:14:05,307 --> 00:14:11,067
Therefore, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ married Rasool Allah ﷺ to Ayesha(عائشه),

164
00:14:11,355 --> 00:14:16,619
at the same age we put our children in school, at the age of six.

165
00:14:17,146 --> 00:14:20,492
Because she was to become the student of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

166
00:14:21,514 --> 00:14:26,250
And for her to fulfill that duty of teaching the Ummah(امة)

167
00:14:26,387 --> 00:14:32,371
and conveying the knowledge of Hadith(حديث) to us, and she didn't have any children

168
00:14:33,551 --> 00:14:39,584
so by the age of 18, Rasool Allah ﷺ has already passed away, and she has no children,

169
00:14:39,966 --> 00:14:45,183
so she could devote her time, full time to teaching the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

170
00:14:45,299 --> 00:14:50,902
Therefore, Ayesha رضي الله عنها ranks Number four among the top narrators of Hadith(حديث).

171
00:14:52,874 --> 00:14:56,282
Among the top narrators of Hadith(حديث), Ayesha رضي الله عنها is Number four.

172
00:14:56,546 --> 00:15:00,973
There is no book of Hadith(حديث) that can be called the Book of Hadith(حديث) if it doesn't have the Hadith(حديث) of Ayesha(عائشه),

173
00:15:01,328 --> 00:15:03,898
there is no book of Fiqh(فقه) that could be considered the book of Fiqh(فقه)

174
00:15:04,047 --> 00:15:05,789
if it doesn't have the Fatawa(فتوي) of Ayesha(عائشه).

175
00:15:06,047 --> 00:15:08,535
And there is no book of Tafseer(تفسير) that can be called Tafseer(تفسير),

176
00:15:08,793 --> 00:15:11,262
if it doesn't have the Tafseer(تفسير) of Ayesha رضي الله عنها .

177
00:15:11,516 --> 00:15:16,222
Therefore Ayesha رضي الله عنها is the greatest woman scholar that ever lived in this world.

178
00:15:18,430 --> 00:15:22,317
Ayesha رضي الله عنها narrated 2210 Ahadith(احاديث),

179
00:15:23,181 --> 00:15:27,418
and Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم) agreed on 147,

180
00:15:28,075 --> 00:15:35,166
Bukhari(بخاري) narrated 54 Ahadith(احاديث) from Ayesha(عائشه) Muslim(مسلم) narrated 69.

181
00:15:35,745 --> 00:15:41,563
Ayesha رضي الله عنها died at the age of 63, in year, 57 of Al-Hijrah(الهجرة).

182
00:15:44,388 --> 00:15:51,554
Umm Kalsoom(ام كلثوم), the youngest of the children of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) and she was born after he died.

183
00:15:53,452 --> 00:15:57,270
 Before the death of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه,

184
00:15:58,254 --> 00:16:05,429
he was speaking to his daughter Ayesha(عائشه) and he told her, these are you two brothers, and these are your two sisters.

185
00:16:06,756 --> 00:16:10,532
So, Ayesha رضي الله عنها said, I know my two brothers

186
00:16:11,849 --> 00:16:16,450
and here is my one sister, Asmaa(اسماء) who is the other one.

187
00:16:17,597 --> 00:16:19,859
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه said;

188
00:16:20,861 --> 00:16:30,881
The other one is the one in the womb of my wife Habiba(حبيبه) and I believe that it's going to be a daughter.

189
00:16:31,859 --> 00:16:37,127
Now that was before he died and it turned out, as he thought.

190
00:16:37,966 --> 00:16:44,162
So, a few months after he passed away his wife delivered Umm Kalsoom رضي الله عنها.

191
00:16:44,736 --> 00:16:48,246
And Umm Kalsoom(ام كلثوم) was then married to Talha Bin Ubaid Illah(طلحه بن عبيد الله),

192
00:16:48,681 --> 00:16:53,184
another of the 10, who were given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

193
00:16:53,650 --> 00:17:01,457
Infact Az-Zubair(الزبير) and Talha(طلحه) had such a close relationship and a brotherly relationship,

194
00:17:01,922 --> 00:17:05,158
you rarely can mention the name of one without mentioning the name of the other.

195
00:17:05,335 --> 00:17:09,582
So Az-Zubair(الزبير) and Talha(طلحه) always go together and they even died together

196
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:13,221
in the Waqa'a(وقع) of Al-Jamal(الجمل), in the battle of Al-Jamal(الجمل).

197
00:17:14,061 --> 00:17:18,996
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه had his daughter Asmaa(اسماء) married to Az-Zubair(الزبير),

198
00:17:19,365 --> 00:17:24,535
and then after he(ابوبكر) passed away, Talha Bin Ubaid Illah(طلحه بن عبيد الله) married his daughter Umm Kalsoom(ام كلثوم).

199
00:17:25,036 --> 00:17:31,425
Therefore both Az-Zubair(الزبير) and Talha(طلحه) had a family relationship with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

200
00:17:31,801 --> 00:17:34,745
Now she didn't live with her husband for very long because,

201
00:17:35,034 --> 00:17:38,070
Talha Bin Ubaid Illah(طلحه بن عبيد الله) was killed in Waqat Ul Jamal(وقعة الجمل).

202
00:17:39,035 --> 00:17:43,255
So this is the family of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

203
00:17:44,838 --> 00:17:46,462
THE ISLAM OF ABU BAKR(ابوبكر).

204
00:17:48,012 --> 00:17:52,210
And I will narrate the statement of Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) in Al-Bidayah Wan Nihayah(البدائية ونهائيه),

205
00:17:52,644 --> 00:18:00,640
Al-Bidayah Wan Nihayah(البدائية ونهائيه) is the famous monumental work of the great Imam(امام) and scholar Ibn Kathir Damishqi(ابن كثير دمشقي).

206
00:18:01,753 --> 00:18:04,427
The name of this encyclopedia is, The Beginning And The End.

207
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:09,037
And it's literally the beginning to the end.

208
00:18:10,876 --> 00:18:17,405
He started from creation, and he ended with when the people entered into Jannah(جنة) and Naar(النار).

209
00:18:18,624 --> 00:18:21,062
So he started by talking about the story of creation,

210
00:18:21,239 --> 00:18:23,278
and then he talks about the stories of the Ambiyaa(انبياء)

211
00:18:23,434 --> 00:18:28,381
and then the Seerah(سيرة) of Muhammadﷺ, and then all the events of history, up to his time.

212
00:18:28,895 --> 00:18:31,477
And then he spoke about the signs of the Day of Judgment,

213
00:18:31,927 --> 00:18:34,041
the day of Judgment, and then Jannah(جنة) and Naar(النار).

214
00:18:34,543 --> 00:18:39,597
One of the best works of history compiled by the Muslim scholars.

215
00:18:40,074 --> 00:18:44,863
Anyway, he says about this, the Islam of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he says;

216
00:18:45,808 --> 00:18:49,520
The first woman to become Muslim was Khadijah رضي الله عنها,

217
00:18:51,134 --> 00:18:55,567
the first child to become Muslim was Ali Bin Abi Talib رضي الله عنه,

218
00:18:56,567 --> 00:19:01,736
the first slave to become Muslim was Zaid Bin Harissa رضي الله عنه,

219
00:19:02,654 --> 00:19:08,399
and the first free man to become Muslim was Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

220
00:19:08,847 --> 00:19:13,445
And his Islam was more beneficial to the religion than all of the above.

221
00:19:14,017 --> 00:19:18,215
Because he became Muslim when he was a noble man in the society.

222
00:19:18,527 --> 00:19:24,338
So he used his nobility, his strength, his abilities, his skills and his wealth

223
00:19:24,466 --> 00:19:28,329
for the service of the religion, and for the service of Muhammadﷺ.

224
00:19:29,317 --> 00:19:31,303
كَانَ صَدْرً مُقَدِّمًا فِيْ قَوْمِه

225
00:19:31,722 --> 00:19:36,011
He says that he was a noble man, and he was a leader among his people.

226
00:19:37,784 --> 00:19:41,310
وإسلامه كان أنفع  من إسلام من تقدم زكرهم

227
00:19:41,744 --> 00:19:44,842
إذ كان صدرًا معظمًا رعيسًا في قريش

228
00:19:45,072 --> 00:19:48,212
مكرمًا وَصاحبهم و مالٍ وداعيً إلإسلام

229
00:19:48,477 --> 00:19:53,940
وكان محببًا متعلفًا يبزل المال في طاعة الله ورسوله

230
00:19:55,962 --> 00:20:01,525
Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he gave Daw'ah(دعوة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه,

231
00:20:02,314 --> 00:20:13,322
he told him Allahعَزّوجَلّ has sent me as a messenger to warn mankind, and I invite you to Islam.

232
00:20:14,659 --> 00:20:21,516
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه immediately without any hesitation, without any second thoughts, said:

233
00:20:21,563 --> 00:20:24,914
أشهد و الله اله الا الله، واشهدو ان محمد الرسول الله

234
00:20:27,948 --> 00:20:29,373
There's a statement that,

235
00:20:29,854 --> 00:20:31,735
لكل حصانٍ قبوة

236
00:20:32,799 --> 00:20:34,787
For every horse, there's a stumble.

237
00:20:35,573 --> 00:20:43,786
Every horse, no matter how good it is, will one day stumble it happens with the best horses.

238
00:20:45,476 --> 00:20:50,401
But they say, with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, that stumble, never came.

239
00:20:51,382 --> 00:20:57,447
With the other invitations that were given by Rasool Allah ﷺ to the Sahabah(صحابه)

240
00:20:58,256 --> 00:21:04,354
with some of them, it took seconds, with some of them, it took days

241
00:21:05,218 --> 00:21:08,371
with some it took months, with some it took years,

242
00:21:08,542 --> 00:21:14,386
like with Khalid Bin Waleed رضي الله عنه, he had to think about Islam for years,

243
00:21:14,952 --> 00:21:18,035
Amr Bin Aas رضي الله عنه, even the son of Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه,

244
00:21:18,059 --> 00:21:21,838
Abdur Rahmaan Bin Abi Bakr(عبدالرحمن بن ابي بكر), he only became Muslim during Sulh Al-Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه).

245
00:21:22,889 --> 00:21:28,938
But with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه as soon as Rasool Allah ﷺ delivered the invitation to him,

246
00:21:29,250 --> 00:21:32,161
immediately Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه became Muslim.

247
00:21:34,619 --> 00:21:35,517
How come.?

248
00:21:36,446 --> 00:21:37,953
If we may ask the question.

249
00:21:40,235 --> 00:21:44,491
Was it because Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) was a type of person, who could change his mind easily?

250
00:21:45,703 --> 00:21:50,250
Was it because he was a person, who could buy into an argument easily?

251
00:21:51,077 --> 00:21:56,181
That wasn't the personality of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, because if you look at the time of his Khilafah(خلافه),

252
00:21:56,232 --> 00:22:01,018
you could see that! Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه can be as firm as one could be.

253
00:22:02,156 --> 00:22:11,298
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in a few instances would stand up against everyone else,

254
00:22:12,450 --> 00:22:17,461
and would hold firm to his opinion and at the end it would turn out to be, the right opinion.

255
00:22:18,849 --> 00:22:21,822
Like what's happened with the army of Osama Bin Zaid رضي الله عنه

256
00:22:21,846 --> 00:22:23,934
and what happened with Qitaal(قتال) with Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

257
00:22:23,958 --> 00:22:26,603
There was a lot of resistance from the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

258
00:22:26,941 --> 00:22:30,015
and they used every convincing argument they could use,

259
00:22:30,301 --> 00:22:34,496
but in the end Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, his argument prevailed.

260
00:22:35,690 --> 00:22:40,903
So, how come Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, immediately accepted the invitation of Rasool Allah ﷺ?

261
00:22:40,954 --> 00:22:43,045
The reason is because he was ready for it.

262
00:22:44,820 --> 00:22:49,648
He maybe has already thought about that a lot, so he didn't need to sit on it.

263
00:22:50,343 --> 00:22:52,073
He didn't need to give it a second thought.

264
00:22:52,684 --> 00:22:57,300
He didn't need to wait and give it consideration, he was already prepared.

265
00:22:59,556 --> 00:23:04,694
Ayesha رضي الله عنها says my father never ever prostrated to an idol,

266
00:23:06,588 --> 00:23:10,607
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was never a Mushrik(مشرك).

267
00:23:11,627 --> 00:23:19,005
He said: When I was young, my father took me to the idols, where the idols were gathered.

268
00:23:20,347 --> 00:23:21,058
 And he told me,

269
00:23:21,082 --> 00:23:23,794
هذه الهتك شمل العوالي

270
00:23:24,557 --> 00:23:29,500
These are your noble gods and then he left me.

271
00:23:31,151 --> 00:23:36,890
That is how religion is passed on, parents, deliver their religion to their children.

272
00:23:37,415 --> 00:23:42,192
So, the father Abu Qahafah(ابوقحافه) is taking his son Abu Bakr(أبوبكر) to introduce him to the idols, he's saying,

273
00:23:42,376 --> 00:23:43,906
 هذه الهتك شمل العوالي

274
00:23:43,999 --> 00:23:49,524
These are your noble gods, so worship them and then he left his son.

275
00:23:49,979 --> 00:23:54,677
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was speaking to the idols and was saying: Can you benefit me,

276
00:23:55,651 --> 00:23:58,944
can you harm me, can you eat, can you drink.

277
00:23:59,535 --> 00:24:06,184
And then he said: I'm not gonna worship idols that cannot hear or see, when he was a child.

278
00:24:08,290 --> 00:24:09,552
So, he was ready for it.

279
00:24:10,048 --> 00:24:15,958
So, you would find that the people who immediately accepted the message, were the people, who were at some level of preparation

280
00:24:16,253 --> 00:24:17,523
they were waiting for it.

281
00:24:18,108 --> 00:24:21,827
See with some people, they were waiting for it but they could not get there

282
00:24:21,867 --> 00:24:23,694
 because they needed a Nabi(نبي) to deliver to them.

283
00:24:24,465 --> 00:24:28,131
Abu Dhar Al-Ghiffaari رضي الله عنه, when he left his people in Ghifaar(غفار),

284
00:24:29,151 --> 00:24:35,996
they were not businessmen like the people of Makkah nor were they in agriculture like the people of Madina,

285
00:24:36,056 --> 00:24:39,301
their profession was raiding caravans, stealing.

286
00:24:39,944 --> 00:24:46,487
Abu Dhar Al-Ghiffaari(ابوذرالغفاري), his Fitrah(فطرة), his natural disposition told him that this is wrong so he left his people.

287
00:24:48,843 --> 00:24:55,287
When he was passing next to Makkah, he heard the news that there was someone in Makkah who's claiming to be a prophet.

288
00:24:56,042 --> 00:24:58,688
So he sent his brother, Unais(انيس) to check it out.

289
00:24:59,682 --> 00:25:04,450
Unais(انيس) came back to him and said that people say that he's a magician, some say that he's ... about Muhammadﷺ.

290
00:25:04,708 --> 00:25:07,465
Some say, he's a liar, some say he's a poet, some say he is insane,

291
00:25:07,887 --> 00:25:11,468
he's possessed with demons, he is this, he is a fortune teller, he is this and that.

292
00:25:12,465 --> 00:25:14,119
Abu Dhar Al-Ghiffaari رضي الله عنه said,

293
00:25:14,144 --> 00:25:15,137
ما أغنَيْتَ عَنِّيْ شيئا

294
00:25:15,162 --> 00:25:18,169
You haven't done me any good, I'm going to go and check it out myself.

295
00:25:18,698 --> 00:25:23,248
And he went into Makkah and he had a meeting with Rasool Allah ﷺ and he immediately became a Muslim. Why.?

296
00:25:24,097 --> 00:25:27,050
Abu Dhar Al-Ghiffaari رضي الله عنه says about himself

297
00:25:27,347 --> 00:25:31,895
that I used to pray to Allahعَزّوجَلّ, two years before I became a Muslim.

298
00:25:33,410 --> 00:25:38,127
Two years before I became a Muslim, I used to pray to Allahعَزّوجَلّ, so they asked him,

299
00:25:38,318 --> 00:25:39,288
How would you do that.?

300
00:25:39,475 --> 00:25:42,469
He would say: I would face whichever direction, I can.

301
00:25:42,955 --> 00:25:45,384
And I would pray, how ever, I could.

302
00:25:46,271 --> 00:25:49,821
He didn't know how to pray, Salawaat Ul Khams(صلواة الخمس),

303
00:25:50,117 --> 00:25:54,435
because to do that you need the guidance of the Nabi(نبي) - Muhammadﷺ.

304
00:25:55,246 --> 00:25:59,549
But his Fitrah(فطرة) was telling him that the truth is the oneness of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

305
00:26:01,461 --> 00:26:09,495
Salman Al-Farisi رضي الله عنه, he immediately accepted the message of Muhammadﷺ because he was waiting for it.

306
00:26:10,705 --> 00:26:15,265
So that was the stage of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he was waiting for it,

307
00:26:15,289 --> 00:26:18,501
therefore as soon as the invitation came, he immediately accepted it.

308
00:26:20,294 --> 00:26:22,680
Like when you're waiting for something so bad and

309
00:26:23,255 --> 00:26:26,200
as soon as the invitation comes, you immediately respond.

310
00:26:28,448 --> 00:26:36,030
Not only in terms of Tauheed(توحيد), the character of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), his character, his makeup was good from the beginning.

311
00:26:37,781 --> 00:26:45,805
Ayesha رضي الله عنه says about her father, that my father did not drink alcohol in Islam, or before Islam

312
00:26:46,779 --> 00:26:47,847
he didn't drink Khamr(خمر).

313
00:26:48,711 --> 00:26:51,225
In another narration Ayesha رضي الله عنها says that

314
00:26:51,283 --> 00:26:57,084
my father and Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان إبن عفان) called Alcohol Haraam(حرام) from the time of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة),

315
00:26:58,368 --> 00:27:02,215
They did not drink from the time of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة), and they considered it to be Haram(حرام), illegal.

316
00:27:02,761 --> 00:27:06,349
Now why did Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه take that position towards alcohol?

317
00:27:06,669 --> 00:27:15,196
Ayesha رضي الله عنها narrates that once, my father was asked by some Muslims.

318
00:27:15,542 --> 00:27:19,460
Did you drink Khamr(خمر), did you drink wine, when you were a Mushrik(مشرك).?

319
00:27:20,335 --> 00:27:22,048
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

320
00:27:22,088 --> 00:27:23,019
 "أعوذ بالله"

321
00:27:23,171 --> 00:27:27,478
I seek refuge in Allah, they said: How come you say that.?

322
00:27:27,867 --> 00:27:28,978
He said: Because,

323
00:27:29,075 --> 00:27:32,041
كنت أسونوإرضي ومُروعتي

324
00:27:32,647 --> 00:27:35,205
I used to guard my honor and my dignity.

325
00:27:35,568 --> 00:27:40,517
Because drinking violates the honor of a person and violates the dignity of a person.

326
00:27:40,928 --> 00:27:45,254
And Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: One day, I saw a man, who was drunk.

327
00:27:46,227 --> 00:27:55,678
This man would stick his hand in stool, feces, and he would take some of it and try to eat it.

328
00:27:56,533 --> 00:27:59,141
But when he would pull his hand close to his mouth.

329
00:27:59,692 --> 00:28:04,687
He would smell, the bad smell of his stool so he would push his hand away,

330
00:28:04,980 --> 00:28:08,178
but then he would drive his hand closer, and the smell would repel him,

331
00:28:08,860 --> 00:28:13,212
and he would keep on doing that, and the smell is repulsing him, otherwise he would eat from it.

332
00:28:13,695 --> 00:28:15,030
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

333
00:28:15,070 --> 00:28:16,313
 "إنَّ هذا رجل لا يعقل"

334
00:28:16,552 --> 00:28:20,590
This man has no sense, he lost his mind.

335
00:28:21,107 --> 00:28:24,805
And that is what alcohol does to you, you lose your mind.

336
00:28:25,286 --> 00:28:27,030
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

337
00:28:27,055 --> 00:28:29,685
كنت أسونوإرضي ومُروعتي

338
00:28:30,040 --> 00:28:34,192
I used to protect my dignity and my honor and he did this, before Islam.

339
00:28:36,564 --> 00:28:44,937
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, also had the character of a Da'iyah(داعية), a caller to Islam.

340
00:28:45,847 --> 00:28:48,548
And this is what Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) talks about.

341
00:28:49,255 --> 00:28:55,098
Abu Bakr As-siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), when he came into Islam, he came in with everything that he had,

342
00:28:55,215 --> 00:28:57,700
 he put everything on the line for the service of Islam.

343
00:29:00,679 --> 00:29:09,331
Very soon after he became Muslim, he started inviting others towards Islam

344
00:29:10,111 --> 00:29:15,224
and look at the names that he brought into the fold of the religion.

345
00:29:16,260 --> 00:29:20,350
Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه, Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(الزبيربن عوام),

346
00:29:21,176 --> 00:29:24,539
Talha Bin Ubaid Illah(طلحه بن عبيدالله), Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف),

347
00:29:25,262 --> 00:29:29,392
Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدابن ابي وقاص) and Abi Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(ابوعبيده عمروبن جراح).

348
00:29:29,998 --> 00:29:34,660
All of these five are among the 10, who are given glad tidings of Jannah(جنة),

349
00:29:34,938 --> 00:29:38,215
and they became Muslim through the Da'wah(دعوة) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

350
00:29:39,305 --> 00:29:45,849
Therefore, everything they do, a copy of that will go into the account of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه on the Day of Judgment.

351
00:29:46,669 --> 00:29:52,769
Five of the 10, who were given glad tidings of Jannah(جنة) became Muslim through the Da'wah(دعوة) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق),

352
00:29:52,852 --> 00:29:55,890
not only that but there are many others, I just mentioned the names of these

353
00:29:56,222 --> 00:29:59,322
because these are among the 10, but also Al-Arqam Ibn Al-Arqam(ارقم ابن الارقم)

354
00:29:59,566 --> 00:30:01,057
became Muslim, due to the Da'wah(دعوة) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

355
00:30:01,576 --> 00:30:04,939
the house where Rasool Allah ﷺ would meet in Makkah, Daar Ul Arqam(دارالارقم).

356
00:30:05,599 --> 00:30:09,746
Abu Salamah Bin Abd Asad(ابوسلمه بن عبدالاسد) also became Muslim through the Da'wah(دعوة) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

357
00:30:10,156 --> 00:30:15,972
So he was a blessed man and this relates to the personality of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

358
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:21,878
He was very social, very likable, very approachable.

359
00:30:22,574 --> 00:30:29,118
He was very good in his social skills, he had a very wide social network,

360
00:30:29,740 --> 00:30:34,902
very well known all over Arabia, he knows a lot about others.

361
00:30:35,531 --> 00:30:39,062
Therefore this opens the lines of communication between him and other tribes.

362
00:30:39,086 --> 00:30:45,263
See, when you know about the background of the people that facilitates, your conversation with them.

363
00:30:45,587 --> 00:30:47,033
 So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique  رضي الله عنه.

364
00:30:47,058 --> 00:30:47,845
كان نصابة

365
00:30:48,447 --> 00:30:50,874
He was a scholar of his time in genealogy.

366
00:30:51,222 --> 00:30:56,401
So, he knew the names of the tribes, their locations, their qualities, the pros and cons of each tribe,

367
00:30:56,788 --> 00:30:59,682
 and you can find that he is very prevalent in his discussions with others.

368
00:31:03,085 --> 00:31:10,443
Naturally Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, had to go through the persecution that the Muslims, went through.

369
00:31:12,505 --> 00:31:19,010
Allahسبحانه وتعالى tested them, and He tested him, like everyone else.

370
00:31:20,895 --> 00:31:25,308
When the Muslims reached 38 in number.

371
00:31:27,608 --> 00:31:31,521
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه went to Muhammadﷺ and said;

372
00:31:32,711 --> 00:31:37,170
Messenger of Allah! We should proclaim the message publicly,

373
00:31:39,291 --> 00:31:43,059
up to that stage, the Da'wah(دعوة) was done, secretly.

374
00:31:44,392 --> 00:31:48,367
Rasool Allah ﷺ would invite his close associates.

375
00:31:48,902 --> 00:31:53,469
People whom he trusts, and he would never make a public announcement of it.

376
00:31:54,144 --> 00:31:58,056
Because of the danger and risk in those early days of Da'wah(دعوة).

377
00:32:00,026 --> 00:32:03,578
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه felt that we have reached a stage

378
00:32:03,864 --> 00:32:08,751
where our numbers qualify us to publicly proclaim the message.

379
00:32:09,723 --> 00:32:12,144
So, he goes to Muhammadﷺ and says,

380
00:32:12,505 --> 00:32:19,524
O Messenger of Allah, We want to make Istelaan(إستعلان), Istalan(إستعلن), make the message public.

381
00:32:19,826 --> 00:32:21,951
Rasool Allah ﷺ responded by saying,

382
00:32:21,991 --> 00:32:23,170
"إنَّ قليل"

383
00:32:23,624 --> 00:32:25,524
We are few, in number.

384
00:32:26,381 --> 00:32:33,120
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه kept on insisting on Rasool Allah ﷺ, until the Messenger of Allah agreed.

385
00:32:34,116 --> 00:32:37,814
Rasool Allah ﷺ would lend an open ear to the advice of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق),

386
00:32:39,198 --> 00:32:41,499
the relationship between them was so close.

387
00:32:42,440 --> 00:32:47,628
And only Allah knows the conversations that went between them,

388
00:32:47,708 --> 00:32:52,395
see Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه has not narrated many Ahadith(احاديث),

389
00:32:52,987 --> 00:32:59,878
because Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه passed away very early on, in Islam, two years after the death of Muhammadﷺ.

390
00:33:00,849 --> 00:33:03,691
So, we really don't know what went on between them.

391
00:33:03,744 --> 00:33:09,839
I mean, Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) has spent hours and hours and hours together, a lot of time.

392
00:33:11,245 --> 00:33:15,118
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ accepted the advice of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

393
00:33:15,840 --> 00:33:19,970
So, they went into the Masjid(مسجد), where all of the Mushrikeen(مشركين) are gathered

394
00:33:21,036 --> 00:33:23,459
and the Sahabah(صحابه) spread around the Masjid(مسجد),

395
00:33:24,273 --> 00:33:27,886
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting next to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), while Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was standing.

396
00:33:28,351 --> 00:33:31,614
And Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه delivered the speech,

397
00:33:31,876 --> 00:33:35,872
and that was the first public speech ever delivered in Islam.

398
00:33:36,369 --> 00:33:39,546
Therefore Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) is not only the first Muslim

399
00:33:41,386 --> 00:33:44,480
and the first after the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) to enter into Jannah(جنة),

400
00:33:45,277 --> 00:33:48,290
and the greatest of the Al-Mo'minoon(مؤمنون), and the first Khalifah(خليفه),

401
00:33:48,576 --> 00:33:51,767
but he's also the first public speaker in Islam.

402
00:33:53,224 --> 00:33:57,462
He stood up and he proclaimed the Shahadah(شهادة) of,

403
00:33:57,954 --> 00:34:01,584
"لا اله الا الله محمد رسول الله "

404
00:34:02,444 --> 00:34:06,911
You can obviously imagine the response.

405
00:34:08,578 --> 00:34:13,865
The Mushrikeen(مشركين) attacked, and their point of attack was.?

406
00:34:14,611 --> 00:34:16,981
The speaker! Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق).

407
00:34:18,352 --> 00:34:19,315
They all jumped on him.

408
00:34:20,820 --> 00:34:25,755
They did attack the others but the focus of their attack was Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه.

409
00:34:27,861 --> 00:34:30,788
Among the attackers was Ut'ba Bin Rabiyah(عتبة بن ربيعة),

410
00:34:31,702 --> 00:34:38,981
who after he threw Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to the ground, he took off his shoes

411
00:34:40,236 --> 00:34:45,914
and he started hitting Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in the face, and pressing the shoes in the face of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

412
00:34:46,854 --> 00:34:55,719
And it wasn't until Bannu Taim(بنوتيم), the tribe of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) came in and interfered and pushed away the attackers,

413
00:34:56,087 --> 00:34:59,340
the attack stopped, otherwise Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) would have died.

414
00:34:59,822 --> 00:35:01,958
Because they have disfigured his face

415
00:35:02,122 --> 00:35:07,059
so you cannot tell his nose, from the rest of the face, covered in blood.

416
00:35:08,354 --> 00:35:15,164
They carried him back home, and the men of Taim(تيم), alongside the father of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) were standing around him.

417
00:35:15,432 --> 00:35:17,010
They thought that his death was certain.

418
00:35:17,616 --> 00:35:24,310
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, his face was disfigured, body injured, and he lost consciousness.

419
00:35:25,813 --> 00:35:29,717
So they went to Ut'ba(عتبة), and they said;

420
00:35:30,785 --> 00:35:34,169
If our man dies then we're going to kill Ut'ba(عتبة).

421
00:35:35,131 --> 00:35:38,908
And that would have sparked a war in Quraish(قريش),

422
00:35:38,948 --> 00:35:45,135
because you know the tribal system, you kill one of ours, we kill one of yours, that's how it works.

423
00:35:45,792 --> 00:35:49,368
 This is serious, among tribes, they don't take this lightly.

424
00:35:49,927 --> 00:35:55,522
Bannu Taim(بنوتيم) even though, they were considered to be a small clan in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), not one of the strong clans.

425
00:35:55,950 --> 00:35:59,516
But they said if our man dies and even though these were all Mushrikeen(مشركين),

426
00:35:59,761 --> 00:36:01,917
if our man dies, we're gonna kill Ut'ba(عتبة).

427
00:36:04,606 --> 00:36:08,143
Hours later, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) regained consciousness.

428
00:36:09,444 --> 00:36:10,917
And what was the first thing he said;

429
00:36:12,624 --> 00:36:14,557
ما فعل رسول الله

430
00:36:14,835 --> 00:36:17,175
What happened to Rasool Allah ﷺ.?

431
00:36:18,733 --> 00:36:21,064
What happened to the Messenger of Allah.?

432
00:36:22,963 --> 00:36:26,934
Now you can only imagine the response of Bannu Taim(بنوتيم).

433
00:36:27,825 --> 00:36:31,313
They started cursing Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق), yelling at him.

434
00:36:33,862 --> 00:36:41,720
The way they saw this, is that you got into this trouble because you followed Muhammad ﷺthis man, who brought us disunity.

435
00:36:41,781 --> 00:36:46,907
See the kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they would always accuse Muhammad(محمد) of bringing disunity among them

436
00:36:47,333 --> 00:36:49,899
 and making them break ties to their kinship.

437
00:36:50,264 --> 00:36:55,261
Because in one family, you would have Muslims and non Muslims and that caused the Rift,

438
00:36:56,758 --> 00:37:01,444
from the top of the society down to each individual family.

439
00:37:01,799 --> 00:37:03,683
So, they said, they used to always say,

440
00:37:03,770 --> 00:37:04,751
 "فرَّقَّ جَمَاعْتَنَا"

441
00:37:04,953 --> 00:37:06,835
This is the man, who brought us disunity.

442
00:37:09,892 --> 00:37:16,325
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has called Qur'an, Furqaan(فرقان), it separates between good and evil.

443
00:37:16,931 --> 00:37:21,197
So that break apart was happening, even on the level of the family.

444
00:37:21,588 --> 00:37:25,326
Some people will choose Al-Haqq(الحق), some people will choose Al-Batil(الباطل).

445
00:37:27,607 --> 00:37:33,085
Bannu Taim(بنوتيم) were upset with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه because they said:

446
00:37:33,699 --> 00:37:36,811
 You got into this trouble because of Muhammadﷺ

447
00:37:37,380 --> 00:37:44,286
we were going to have to fight a war if you died because of the trouble of Muhammadﷺ.

448
00:37:44,680 --> 00:37:50,389
And now, as soon as you wake up rather than taking care of yourself and taking care of your tribe.

449
00:37:50,716 --> 00:37:54,997
You ask about what happened to Muhammadﷺ, when you're on the verge of death.

450
00:37:56,054 --> 00:37:59,010
So they were very angered by that statement and they walked out.

451
00:38:00,897 --> 00:38:05,775
And this was very difficult, I mean, that's not pressure that any one of us could handle.

452
00:38:08,593 --> 00:38:10,758
You get into trouble because of Da'wah(دعوة)

453
00:38:10,798 --> 00:38:18,206
and then you are still willing to publicly state that even after all this happened to me,

454
00:38:18,573 --> 00:38:21,090
all what I care about is Muhammadﷺ.

455
00:38:22,333 --> 00:38:29,618
So they left him, Abu Qahafah(ابوقحافه), the father of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه left

456
00:38:29,658 --> 00:38:33,341
and he told the mother of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to feed him.

457
00:38:36,726 --> 00:38:42,745
So the mother of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) brought in, some food and water to her son, Abu Bakr As-Siddique.

458
00:38:44,024 --> 00:38:48,059
He asked her, How is Muhammadﷺ.?

459
00:38:49,695 --> 00:38:53,980
She said: My son I have no idea about Muhammadﷺ, eat some food and drink.

460
00:38:54,938 --> 00:39:04,602
He said: My mother go to Umm Jameel Bint Al-Khattab(أم جميل بنت ألخطاب) and ask her about Muhammadﷺ.

461
00:39:06,383 --> 00:39:10,806
So she went to Umm Jameel(ام جميل), and she asked her.

462
00:39:11,446 --> 00:39:16,623
My son is asking you how is Muhammadﷺ.?

463
00:39:19,057 --> 00:39:24,887
So, she responded by saying and look at the response of Umm Jameel(ام جميل),

464
00:39:25,788 --> 00:39:31,394
because Umm Jameel(ام جميل) was Muslim in secret, it wasn't public.

465
00:39:32,970 --> 00:39:37,872
She said: I have no idea about Muhammadﷺ and I have no idea about your son.

466
00:39:38,509 --> 00:39:39,736
I know nothing about them.

467
00:39:42,275 --> 00:39:46,829
She had to protect herself because, again, in that stage the Muslims were very few and weak

468
00:39:47,721 --> 00:39:50,246
and the mother of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) wasn't Muslim, so she said;

469
00:39:51,239 --> 00:39:56,188
I have no idea about Muhammadﷺ and I have no idea about Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), I don't know anything about them.

470
00:39:57,623 --> 00:40:00,796
 But if you want, I can go and see your son.

471
00:40:01,995 --> 00:40:06,511
So she wants to protect herself but in the same time, she's concerned about Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه.

472
00:40:07,675 --> 00:40:10,003
So she went alongside the mother of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

473
00:40:11,914 --> 00:40:16,780
And Umm Jameel(ام جميل) as soon as she saw Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in the stage, he was in.

474
00:40:17,737 --> 00:40:20,009
She screamed.! And she said;

475
00:40:20,056 --> 00:40:22,286
People who did this to you are an evil people.

476
00:40:23,017 --> 00:40:31,765
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said, O Umm Jameel(ام جميل), how is Muhammadﷺ.?

477
00:40:33,918 --> 00:40:38,478
Umm Jameel(ام جميل) said: Your mother is listening, your mother is here.

478
00:40:39,623 --> 00:40:42,264
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: Don't worry about her, speak.

479
00:40:43,421 --> 00:40:47,703
Even though the mother of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) wasn't Muslim, but his family is trustworthy,

480
00:40:48,523 --> 00:40:50,906
and you can speak in front of my mother.

481
00:40:52,854 --> 00:40:56,576
She said: Muhammadﷺ is healthy and fine.

482
00:40:59,688 --> 00:41:06,858
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: I am not going to eat anything, nor will I drink anything, until you're taking me to him

483
00:41:07,731 --> 00:41:09,552
I want to see Muhammadﷺ.

484
00:41:11,231 --> 00:41:17,881
So, they took Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) at night, hours later,

485
00:41:19,327 --> 00:41:22,006
and they had to carry him because again he cannot even walk.

486
00:41:23,451 --> 00:41:29,111
They had to carry him on their shoulders and it was late at night.

487
00:41:31,283 --> 00:41:36,852
And as soon as they came in to the place where Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه) were sitting,

488
00:41:38,633 --> 00:41:42,491
immediately Rasool Allah ﷺ stood up and kissed Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه,

489
00:41:42,515 --> 00:41:45,498
when he saw his state, and he felt very sorry for him.

490
00:41:47,967 --> 00:41:49,845
What did Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه say.?

491
00:41:51,646 --> 00:41:54,336
Did he say, O Rasool Allah ﷺ, I suffered so much for you.?

492
00:41:55,791 --> 00:41:59,408
O messenger of Allah, I'm, in pain, I'm aching.

493
00:42:00,794 --> 00:42:03,646
O Messenger of Allah, I was about to die.

494
00:42:05,351 --> 00:42:11,053
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: O Messenger of Allah

495
00:42:11,781 --> 00:42:16,325
There is no harm in me, whatsoever, I'm feeling no pain, whatsoever.

496
00:42:16,477 --> 00:42:19,061
It's just this small injury in my face, That's it.!

497
00:42:21,648 --> 00:42:23,467
إِلَّا ابْتِغَاءَ وَجْهِ رَبِّهِ الْأَعْلَىٰ۝

498
00:42:24,705 --> 00:42:27,462
He's doing everything, for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

499
00:42:29,721 --> 00:42:36,011
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, was an example of sacrifice to the limit,

500
00:42:36,715 --> 00:42:38,617
giving everything for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

501
00:42:41,328 --> 00:42:47,734
One of the Sahabah(صحابه) Abdullah Bin Amr Bin Aas(عبدالله بن عمروبن ألعاص) was asked by Tabaeen(تابعين).

502
00:42:48,405 --> 00:42:54,043
What is the worst thing you have seen in the persecution of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) to Muhammadﷺ.?

503
00:42:54,136 --> 00:42:57,334
 What is the worst thing, that you have seen, you have witnessed.?

504
00:42:57,374 --> 00:43:01,770
I mean Rasool Allah ﷺ, went through a lot, but tell us about something that you have witnessed yourself,

505
00:43:01,823 --> 00:43:03,911
Abdullah Bin Amr Bin Aas(عبدالله بن عمروبن ألعاص), one of the early Muslims.

506
00:43:04,878 --> 00:43:10,114
He said: One day, I saw the Mushrikeen(مشركين) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) attack Muhammadﷺ.

507
00:43:11,103 --> 00:43:16,716
And they're grabbing him, pulling him and yelling at him, fighting him.

508
00:43:17,425 --> 00:43:23,346
And then I saw Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه pulling them, and pushing them, away and saying,

509
00:43:23,391 --> 00:43:25,728
أتقتلون الرجل أن يقول ربي الله

510
00:43:25,752 --> 00:43:28,494
Are you killing a man just because he says, My lord is Allah.?

511
00:43:31,068 --> 00:43:32,281
And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ),

512
00:43:33,881 --> 00:43:37,522
and there's another narration that could be talking about the same incident.

513
00:43:38,088 --> 00:43:42,197
Asma Bin Abi Bakr رضي الله عنها said; We're once at home.

514
00:43:42,462 --> 00:43:50,741
 So, somebody came to us and spoke to my father and said: Go and help your friend - Muhammadﷺ.

515
00:43:50,818 --> 00:43:53,043
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) immediately rushed.

516
00:43:53,563 --> 00:43:58,182
Asma(اسماء) said; Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had four braids, they used to tie their hair.

517
00:44:00,449 --> 00:44:07,430
So, he went to help Rasool Allah ﷺ, and he was pushing the people away from Muhammadﷺ alone,

518
00:44:07,498 --> 00:44:10,403
 see this huge group was attacking Muhammadﷺ

519
00:44:10,762 --> 00:44:13,485
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) alone was trying to push them away.

520
00:44:14,192 --> 00:44:14,673
And he's saying

521
00:44:14,697 --> 00:44:16,812
 أتقتلون الرجل أن يقول ربي الله

522
00:44:16,836 --> 00:44:19,715
Are you killing a man, just because he says that Allah is my Lord.

523
